+
+With spare GPU memory, opt into lossless IQ2_XXS expansion at load time:
+
+```bash
+vllm serve <model> --kernel-config '{"modelopt_iq2_expand": true}'
+```
+
+This stores magnitude and sign planes with exact FP32 group scales, reducing
+decode work without changing the decoded weights or quantizing activations.
+IQ2_XXS storage grows from 66 to 128 bytes per 256 values; Q8_0 and other
+formats are unaffected. The default retains checkpoint-sized storage. The
+option applies only to the Triton path; automatic b12x selection is unchanged.
+Include the expanded weights in your `--gpu-memory-utilization` budget.
